I posted one comment, on #982, and kept that issue open.

#982 (comment posted, still open): Two more commands now exit with an error code (1) when given a bad argument, in commit 4770bc05:
• `yoyo tree <bad arg>` used to print its usage line and exit 0.
• `yoyo undo <bad arg>` did the same. Its argument handling is now a single parser that both the REPL command and the CLI command use, so they can't disagree about what a bad argument is.

I checked this on the built binary: tree zz_bad, tree /nonexistent and undo zz went from exit 0 to exit 1. These cases still exit 0 as intended: bare undo, undo 0, and tree / tree 2 inside a repo. The status block at the top of the issue was already updated during the session.

Still open on #982:
• def/outline when nothing is found, and bare run, still exit 0.
• New finding: map <missing path> exits 0, so a missing path looks like an empty project.
• Most commands haven't been tested for this yet, so their status is unknown.

